---@field pushDownPredicates? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field s3TableUseInvalidColumns? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field sessionIdPushdown? boolean|distilled.Null Push a `session_id_v7 IN (SELECT … FROM events WHERE …)` predicate into the raw_sessions subquery to limit aggregation to sessions that participate in the outer events filter.
---@field sessionPropertyPreAggregation? boolean|distilled.Null Pre-filter raw_sessions aggregation by `session_id_v7 IN (cheap pre-aggregation that only materializes the columns referenced by the outer-WHERE session predicate)`. Useful when the breakdown/SELECT pulls in many session columns (e.g. `$channel_type`) but the filter only references one (e.g. `$entry_current_url`).
---@field sessionTableVersion? posthog.marketing_analytics.SessionTableVersion|string|distilled.Null
---@field sessionTimestampBufferMinutes? number|distilled.Null Padding, in minutes, on each side of the event time range when it filters the sessions table by session start. Defaults to 3 days. It can only narrow the range: values above the default are ignored. Lower it only for a query that keeps just the sessions that start inside its own time range.
---@field sessionsV2JoinMode? posthog.marketing_analytics.SessionsV2JoinMode|string|distilled.Null
---@field timings? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field typeAwareCastSimplification? boolean|distilled.Null Remove provably redundant casts and nullability wrappers (e.g. `toString(String)`, `assumeNotNull(non_nullable)`, dead `ifNull` fallbacks) using inferred expression types
---@field useMaterializedViews? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field useNewEventsSchema? boolean|distilled.Null Read events from the native JSON events table (`true`) or the legacy events table (`false`). When unset, a staff person's `ph_new_events_schema` cookie applies, then the project's listing in the `CLICKHOUSE_HOGQL_USE_NEW_EVENTS_SCHEMA_TEAMS` instance setting, then the `CLICKHOUSE_HOGQL_USE_NEW_EVENTS_SCHEMA` instance setting. This is an internal rollout switch, and the project settings API ignores it.
---@field usePreaggregatedIntermediateResults? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field usePreaggregatedTableTransforms? boolean|distilled.Null Try to automatically convert HogQL queries to use preaggregated tables at the AST level *
---@field useWebAnalyticsPreAggregatedTables? boolean|distilled.Null
---@field webAnalyticsFirstPageviewFilters? boolean|distilled.Null Serve filters on the stored session-entry attribution properties (`$channel_type`, `$entry_utm_*`, `$entry_referring_domain`) by recomputing the value from the session's first pageview. Resolved server-side; not intended to be set by clients.

