---Apply setup operations
---
---Apply one or more setup operations from the setup plan, atomically. Either every operation lands or none does — a partially-applied batch has no well-defined undo. Returns `undo_ops`, computed from the pre-change state, which can be POSTed back to reverse the batch. Only send `apply` payloads returned by setup_plan.
---
---`POST /api/projects/{project_id}/marketing_analytics/apply_setup_ops/`
---Errors: BadRequest, NotFound.
---@param input posthog.marketing_analytics.MarketingAnalyticsApplySetupOpsCreateRequest
---@return posthog.marketing_analytics.ApplySetupOpsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:marketing_analytics_apply_setup_ops_create(input) end

---Create conversion goal
---
---Add one conversion goal to the project. The server assigns conversion_goal_id and appends the goal to the end of the list, leaving existing goals untouched.
---
---`POST /api/projects/{project_id}/marketing_analytics/conversion_goals/create/`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden.
---@param input posthog.marketing_analytics.MarketingAnalyticsConversionGoalsCreateCreateRequest
---@return posthog.marketing_analytics.ConversionGoalWriteResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:marketing_analytics_conversion_goals_create_create(input) end

---Update conversion goal
---
---Change one conversion goal in place. Fields you send are merged into the stored goal, the rest are kept, and the goal keeps its position in the list. Sending a different `kind` replaces the goal instead, since the shapes don't share their fields.
---
---`PATCH /api/projects/{project_id}/marketing_analytics/conversion_goals/{conversion_goal_id}/update/`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound.
---@param input posthog.marketing_analytics.MarketingAnalyticsConversionGoalsUpdatePartialUpdateRequest
---@return posthog.marketing_analytics.ConversionGoalWriteResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:marketing_analytics_conversion_goals_update_partial_update(input) end

